# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite dev server — backend wiring
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the dev server proxies /api and /ws requests to. The default
# (used by `npm run dev:local`) points at the local docker-compose stack.
# Override with one of the presets below, or your own URL.
#
# Local docker-compose (default — start `docker compose up` first):
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
#
# Tailnet gateway (recommended when your Mac is on the tailnet):
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://ircfiber-prod-1.tail544547.ts.net
#
# Different tailnet host / port-forwarded port / staging URL:
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://ircfiber-prod-2.tail544547.ts.net
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://100.64.10.20:8090
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://staging.ircfiber.com
#
# The WebSocket URL defaults to the same host with the ws/wss scheme.
# Override separately only when the two endpoints diverge:
#   VITE_BACKEND_WS_URL=wss://ircfiber-prod-1.tail544547.ts.net/ws
VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
VITE_BACKEND_WS_URL=
